.TH KAGI-HOST 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-host \- run a host-local object service and inspect disk placement
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-host
.RB [ \-c " " \fIFILE\fR ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Maps keys to the disks configured for one host and stores objects locally.
Use
.BR kagi-cluster-host (1)
for distributed metadata, recovery, snapshots, or block volumes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Read host YAML from
.IR FILE .
The default is
.IR /etc/kagi/host.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the command list, or use
.I command
.B \-\-help
for command-specific arguments.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the Kagi version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the host-local HTTP service.
.TP
.B validate
Validate the disk paths and identity markers.
Create missing markers and local storage directories.
.TP
.B status
Print the host and cluster identity, keyspace settings, and disk status as JSON.
.TP
.B disks
Print the configured disks and available disk information.
.TP
.BI "locate " KEY
Print the 64-bit position, slot, and selected disk for
.IR KEY .
.TP
.BI "put " "KEY FILE"
Write the contents of
.I FILE
to the local object identified by
.IR KEY .
.TP
.BI "get " "KEY OUTPUT"
Read a local object and write it to
.IR OUTPUT .
.TP
.BI "delete " KEY
Delete the local object identified by
.IR KEY .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-cluster-host (1),
.BR kagi-config (1)
